  "verbalization": "Rilpivirine, through its inclusion in non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors (NRTIs), is linked to Delavirdine, which binds to Cyp2c19. This relationship is supported by multiple paths that converge on the shared classification of Rilpivirine and Delavirdine as organonitrogen heterocyclic compounds and NRTIs. The evidence suggests that Rilpivirine, as part of the NRTI class, may share a mechanism of action with Delavirdine, which directly interacts with Cyp2c19. The lowest common ancestors of Rilpivirine and Delavirdine, both classified under organonitrogen heterocyclic compounds and NRTIs, indicate a structural and functional link that could explain the interaction between Rilpivirine and Cyp2c19. The integration of these paths highlights a potential dependency on cytochrome P450 2C19, which is a key enzyme in drug metabolism, suggesting that Rilpivirine may influence Cyp2c19 activity through its pharmacological properties.",
